   "from": "Duncan Garmonsway",
   "author": "a7af03e957d7de31",
   "date": "2016-06-03T21:12:47Z",
   "subject": "Renege",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Is there an obvious way for arrivals to renege?<div><br></div><div>It&#39;s related to this issue: <a href=\"https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/49\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/49&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468037948000&amp;usg=AOvVaw07OLyZqTqR0Fe1AjY5O_Cz\">https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/49</a>, but with the important difference that reneging occurs between entering a queue and being served, rather than when rejected from a finite queue.  There&#39;s a SimPy example &quot;Reneging (or abandoning) customers&quot; here: <a href=\"https://pythonhosted.org/SimPy/Tutorials/TheBank2.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://pythonhosted.org/SimPy/Tutorials/TheBank2.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468037948000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1KuT-KoxwZsAH56t7Ht4QS\">https://pythonhosted.org/SimPy/Tutorials/TheBank2.html</a>.</div><div><br></div><div>I don&#39;t think this can be implemented by branching, but you might have a genius suggestion.</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "dgbnBjdlBAAJ",
   "from": "Iñaki Úcar",
   "author": "0f5b7adb7e70bd8b",
   "date": "2016-06-04T18:27:28Z",
   "subject": "Re: [simmer-devel] Renege",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">No, definitely it&#39;s not possible to renege right now, and it&#39;s an interesting feature. I&#39;ve opened <a href=\"https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/58\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/58&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468037949000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Vki5P74lzXQmNqlXnQoJy\">an issue</a>. Ideas are welcome.<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">2016-06-03 23:12 GMT+02:00 Duncan Garmonsway <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nacn...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span>:<br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Is there an obvious way for arrivals to renege?<div><br></div><div>It&#39;s related to this issue: <a href=\"https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/49\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/49&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468037949000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3DJVZ-KOgOWtpfSaRUpdoB\">https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/49</a>, but with the important difference that reneging occurs between entering a queue and being served, rather than when rejected from a finite queue.  There&#39;s a SimPy example &quot;Reneging (or abandoning) customers&quot; here: <a href=\"https://pythonhosted.org/SimPy/Tutorials/TheBank2.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://pythonhosted.org/SimPy/Tutorials/TheBank2.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468037949000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1dN_PPNYhClZ3VVbTpd4AV\">https://pythonhosted.org/SimPy/Tutorials/TheBank2.html</a>.</div><div><br></div><div>I don&#39;t think this can be implemented by branching, but you might have a genius suggestion.</div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
