     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I agree that renege would be useful.  As a first pass hack in the mean time - what about subdividing the queue into multiple processes, with a branch at each transition where the entity could either exit the system (if the wait time ended up being long) or continue?</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sat, Jun 4, 2016 at 11:27 AM, Iñaki Úcar <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">i.uc...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">No, definitely it&#39;s not possible to renege right now, and it&#39;s an interesting feature. I&#39;ve opened <a href=\"https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/58\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/58&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468037954000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2faRJOc_RtJGww3vU13Qsl\">an issue</a>. Ideas are welcome.<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">2016-06-03 23:12 GMT+02:00 Duncan Garmonsway <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nacn...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span>:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Is there an obvious way for arrivals to renege?<div><br></div><div>It&#39;s related to this issue: <a href=\"https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/49\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/49&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468037954000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0mKIuv1w5qK1QuSdkeMn3V\">https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/49</a>, but with the important difference that reneging occurs between entering a queue and being served, rather than when rejected from a finite queue.  There&#39;s a SimPy example &quot;Reneging (or abandoning) customers&quot; here: <a href=\"https://pythonhosted.org/SimPy/Tutorials/TheBank2.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://pythonhosted.org/SimPy/Tutorials/TheBank2.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468037954000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Kw6iMoXvWWzx-iKtsTcxK\">https://pythonhosted.org/SimPy/Tutorials/TheBank2.html</a>.</div><div><br></div><div>I don&#39;t think this can be implemented by branching, but you might have a genius suggestion.</div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;simmer-devel&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">simmer-devel...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">simmer...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/simmer-devel/cc4aed45-f5e0-495e-8859-bcc6b048bcb9%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/simmer-devel/cc4aed45-f5e0-495e-8859-bcc6b048bcb9%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468037954000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2_f9ICAjkWhQ2XykI-H3Bl\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/simmer-devel/cc4aed45-f5e0-495e-8859-bcc6b048bcb9%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.goog